# RULE 0 — Work on local Supabase. Never damage production.

This project is the School Management System of the Schools Division of Bayugan City (DepEd).
The production database holds real learner records — names, LRNs, birthdates, health data.
There is no staging copy and no snapshot to roll back to.

A full local Supabase stack, cloned from production, is the **only** database you may connect to —
while coding, while testing, while debugging.

| | Local (use this) | Production (never) |
|---|---|---|
| API | `http://127.0.0.1:54321` | `https://<ref>.supabase.co` |
| Postgres | `postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres` | `db.<ref>.supabase.co` |
| Env file | `.env.development.local` | `.env.local` |

Start it with `npx supabase start`; read the keys back with `npx supabase status` (local demo keys,
safe to paste anywhere).

## Never

- Connect to production at all — not a `SELECT`, not a "quick count", not schema introspection, not
  a browser session logged into the live app. Reading real learner data is a privacy exposure even
  when it changes nothing.
- Read, print, source, or point a script at `.env.local`. It holds the live credentials.
  (`npm run dev` is safe only because `.env.development.local` overrides it.)
- Use a hosted-Supabase MCP server, `supabase link`, `--linked`, `--project-ref`, `db push`,
  `db pull`, `db remote`, or `--db-url` pointing at `*.supabase.co`. The project is deliberately
  unlinked; leave it that way.
- Print or pass the production `NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` — it bypasses every RLS policy.
- Apply a migration to production. That is the user's job. Test locally, hand over the file, and say
  what it changes and how many rows it touches.

## Fine — on local only

Seeding, test data, `DELETE`, `TRUNCATE`, `DROP`, `UPDATE` without a `WHERE`, `supabase db reset`,
recreating a table. That is exactly what the clone exists for. **"I was only testing" is not a
defence against doing any of it to production.**

## Migrations

Immutable and additive. Never edit an already-applied file in `supabase/migrations/` — write a new
numbered one. Prefer `ADD COLUMN` / new table / new policy, guard with `IF EXISTS` / `IF NOT EXISTS`,
preserve existing rows.

**If you are unsure whether an action would reach production, stop and ask.** "It's only a read" is
not an exception, and neither is "the task seems to require it".

Full detail: `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md`, RULE 0.
